  "findings": [
    {
      "description": "IDOR: show_invoice fetches invoice by user-supplied invoice_id without verifying that the invoice belongs to the authenticated caller, allowing any logged-in customer to view other customers' invoices and line items. Although the SQL is parameterized, missing authorization on the sensitive data path is a security issue.",
      "category": "logic-bug",
      "severity": "high",
      "risk_level": "L2"
    }
  ],
  "decision": "HOLD",
  "fix_description": "IDOR: add ownership authorization before returning invoice data. In show_invoice, after fetching the invoice, check that each invoice belongs to the authenticated caller (e.g., invoice['owner_id'] == request.current_user_id) before returning amount/line_items; otherwise return 403/404. SQL injection is already mitigated by parameterized queries, so the required change is authorization on the sensitive data path. Because this touches a security-sensitive path (risk_level L2), this is marked needs-approval and should not be auto-executed without human approval.",
